From dd49c8945270f2756c9570059141c38a60271d77 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lmoresi <louis.moresi@anu.edu.au>
Date: Sat, 28 Nov 2026 15:01:46 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 8/8] Review: a serial job is dumped too; after a kill only the
 asked processes' empty files stay

The parentage rule of the last commit took a rank's Python children for
helpers. A pytest-xdist worker, or the real rank under a wrapper script, is
such a child, and lost its stack file. Every Python process of the job is
armed again. After a dump request the tidy keeps an empty stack file only
for a process the request went to (the record of a rank that did not
answer); one whose process had exited by then (a compiler, a build) goes.

The dump request went only to the job's descendants, so a Python job the
supervisor started itself (a serial job, no launcher) was never asked and
its stack file stayed empty. It is asked now when it is a process this
module armed; a launcher is not signalled.

test_0063: a serial supervised hang leaves one non-empty stack file (fails
before this change).

Underworld development team with AI support from Claude Code
